# tinyalsa_agmtest

## agm_shared_memory_test

`agm_shared_memory_test` validates tagged `AUDIO_LOAD` parameter handling with
shared memory. The tool allocates a shared-memory buffer, writes a
`CAPI_V2_PARAM_ID_LOAD_DUMMY` payload into it, shares the buffer with tagged
modules using GKV-scoped shared-memory SET, and verifies the result using either
copy-based tagged GET or direct app-side mapped-memory reads.

### Concepts

- `ShmemAlloc` and `ShmemFree` are global TinyALSA mixer controls used to manage
  the shared-memory buffer lifetime.
- `setParamShmemTag` is a global TinyALSA mixer control. It sends
  `tag_id + spf_mem_handle + payload_size + target GKV` to AGM.
- `getParamTag` is a global TinyALSA mixer control. It performs normal
  copy-based tagged GET using `tag_id + target GKV`.
- The same shared-memory SET path is used for externally opened graphs and for
  graphs opened by `agm_shared_memory_test` itself. The difference is graph
  ownership, not the SET API.

### Payload

The test writes this layout into the mapped shared-memory buffer:

```
apm_module_param_data_t
  module_instance_id = 0
  param_id           = CAPI_V2_PARAM_ID_LOAD_DUMMY
  param_size         = sizeof(capi_v2_load_dummy_t + array)

capi_v2_load_dummy_t
  num                = write_count
  array[i]           = i
```

### Common Options

```
-D <card>              Mixer/PCM card, default 100
-u <size>              Allocate shared memory
-w <count>             Write dummy payload with count uint32_t values
-T <tag_id>            Tagged module id to target
-gkv <key=value,...>   Explicit target graph GKV
-P2                    Shared-memory tagged SET
-Q2 <count>            Copy-based tagged GET and compare
-R2 <count>            Direct mapped-memory read and compare
--interactive, -I      Enter interactive prompt
```

### Interactive Commands

The interactive prompt is useful when one shared-memory allocation must remain
alive while it is shared with multiple graphs. Use the command reference below
with the external and owner examples in the next sections.

```
Common shared-memory setup:
  help
    Print the interactive command list.

  status
    Show current tag, shared-memory allocation state, selected target, and
    owner graph state.

  tag <tag_id>
    Set the module tag id used by set/get commands.
    Example: tag 0xC00FF022

  alloc <size>
    Allocate shared memory using the global ShmemAlloc mixer control.
    Example: alloc 2097152

  write <count>
    Write the test payload into the allocated shared memory. The payload uses
    count uint32_t values with array[i] = i.
    Example: write 8

External graph mode commands:

graph is opened by another app, for example agmplay

  gkv <gkv>
    Set an unnamed external graph target using GKV. Use this for quick testing
    when only one external graph needs to be controlled.
    Example: gkv skv=0xA1000001,dkv=0xA2000016,dppkv=0xAC000002,vmid=0xDD000001

  target add <name> <gkv>
    Save an external graph target with a readable name. This lets the same app
    session switch between multiple externally opened graphs.
    Example: target add graph1 skv=0xA1000001,dkv=0xA2000016,dppkv=0xAC000002,vmid=0xDD000001

  target use <name>
    Select a previously saved external target as the current set/get target.
    Example: target use graph1

  target list
    List all saved external graph targets and show which one is current.

  set
    Send the shared-memory handle to the currently selected external graph.
    Requires tag, allocated memory, written payload, and selected GKV target.

  get <count> [start]
    Perform copy-based tagged GET from the currently selected graph and compare
    the returned values against the test payload. start is optional and means
    the starting array index.
    Example: get 8
    Example: get 4 2
```

External Graph Mode Example:

Use this when another process owns the graph, such as `agmplay`. Start the graph
first from the external app, then keep `agm_shared_memory_test` alive and share
the same memory handle to one or more graph targets.

graph open/start by external app

```
adb shell agmplay /data/samples_per_sec_all_channels_48KHz_16bit_8ch_2min.wav \
  -D 100 -d 100 -i PCM_RT_PROXY-RX-2 \
  -dkv 0xA2000016 -skv 0xA1000001 -dppkv 0xAC000002 \
  -vmid_kv 0xDD000001 -c 8

adb shell agmplay /data/samples_per_sec_all_channels_48KHz_16bit_8ch_2min.wav \
  -D 100 -d 104 -i TDM-LPAIF_AUD-RX-PRIMARY \
  -dkv 0xA2000017 -skv 0xA1000001 -ikv 1 \
  -vmid_kv 0xDD000001 -c 8
```

Interactive controller:

```
agm_shared_memory_test -D 100 -u 2097152 -w 8 -T 0xC00FF022 --interactive
```

Prompt sequence:

```
target add graph1 skv=0xA1000001,dkv=0xA2000016,dppkv=0xAC000002,vmid=0xDD000001
set
get 8

target add graph2 skv=0xA1000001,dkv=0xA2000017,ikv=1,vmid=0xDD000001
set
get 8

read 8
exit
```

Flow:

```
external app opens graph
agm_shared_memory_test allocates and maps shared memory
target add/use selects graph by GKV
set -> setParamShmemTag -> AGM finds opened graph by GKV -> DSP module receives shared-memory payload
get -> getParamTag -> copy-based tagged GET from selected graph
exit -> free shared memory only; external graphs are not stopped by this app
```

Owner graph mode commands:

graph is opened and controlled by this test app

```
  graph add <name> -d <dev> -i <intf> -skv <kv> -dkv <kv> [owner opts]
    Save an owner graph configuration with a readable name. The graph is owned
    by this test app, so the app can open/start/stop/close it.
    Required options are PCM device, interface name, stream KV, and device KV.
    Optional owner opts include -dppkv, -ikv, -vmid_kv, -offload, --channels,
    --rate, and --bits.
    Example: graph add graph1 -d 100 -i PCM_RT_PROXY-RX-2 -skv 0xA1000001 -dkv 0xA2000016 -dppkv 0xAC000002 -vmid_kv 0xDD000001 --channels 8

  graph use <name>
    Select a saved owner graph as the current graph target.
    Example: graph use graph1

  graph list
    List all saved owner graphs and show open/start state.

  graph open [name]
    Open the selected owner graph, or the named graph if name is provided.
    This programs metadata, connects stream to interface, and calls pcm_open.
    Example: graph open graph1

  graph set [name]
    Share the current shared-memory handle with the selected owner graph, or
    the named graph if name is provided. If the graph is not open yet, this
    command opens it first.
    Example: graph set graph1

  graph start [name]
    Start the selected owner graph, or the named graph if name is provided.
    If the graph is not open yet, this command opens it first.
    Example: graph start graph1

  graph stop [name]
    Stop the selected owner graph, or the named graph if name is provided.
    Example: graph stop graph1

  graph close [name]
    Close the selected owner graph, or the named graph if name is provided.
    This stops the graph if needed, disconnects the stream, and closes PCM.
    Example: graph close graph1
```

Owner Graph Mode Example:

Use this when `agm_shared_memory_test` should open and control the graph. The app
can manage multiple owner graphs in one interactive session and share the same
memory handle to each graph.

Start the prompt:

```
agm_shared_memory_test -D 100 -u 2097152 -w 8 -T 0xC00FF022 --interactive
```

Prompt sequence:

```
graph add graph1 -d 100 -i PCM_RT_PROXY-RX-2 -skv 0xA1000001 -dkv 0xA2000016 -dppkv 0xAC000002 -vmid_kv 0xDD000001 --channels 8
graph set graph1
graph start graph1

graph add graph2 -d 104 -i TDM-LPAIF_AUD-RX-PRIMARY -skv 0xA1000001 -dkv 0xA2000017 -ikv 1 -vmid_kv 0xDD000001 --channels 8
graph set graph2
graph start graph2

graph list
get 8
read 8
exit
```

Recommended order for each owner graph:

```
graph add
graph set     opens the graph if needed, then shares memory
graph start
```

Flow:

```
graph add -> parse owner graph options and infer target GKV
graph set -> owner_graph_open if needed -> pcm_open -> setParamShmemTag -> AGM finds graph by GKV
graph start -> pcm_start
graph stop/close or exit -> pcm_stop, disconnect, pcm_close
```

```
Verification and session control:
  read <count> [start]
    Read directly from the app's mapped shared-memory virtual address and
    compare values against the test payload. start is optional and means the
    starting array index.
    Example: read 8
    Example: read 4 2

  sleep <ms>
    Pause the interactive session for the requested time.
    Example: sleep 100

  exit
    Exit the prompt. Owner graphs opened by this app are stopped/closed during
    cleanup, and shared memory is freed if the free flag is enabled.
```

### Batch Mode

Batch mode is useful for automation or for a single-shot validation command.
The tool processes command-line options in the exact order they are given, and
most options execute immediately when parsed. Because of that, prerequisites
must appear before the operation that needs them. For example, allocate memory
with `-u` before `-w`, set the tag and target GKV before `-P2` or `-Q2`, and in
owner mode use `-P2` before `--start-graph` if the memory should be shared
before the graph starts.

External graph example:

```
agm_shared_memory_test -D 100 -u 2097152 -w 8 -T 0xC00FF022 \
  -gkv skv=0xA1000001,dkv=0xA2000016,dppkv=0xAC000002,vmid=0xDD000001 \
  -P2 -Q2 8 -R2 8 -f 1
```

Owner graph example:

```
agm_shared_memory_test --open-graph \
  -D 100 -d 100 -i PCM_RT_PROXY-RX-2 \
  -skv 0xA1000001 -dkv 0xA2000016 -dppkv 0xAC000002 \
  -vmid_kv 0xDD000001 --channels 8 --rate 48000 --bits 16 \
  -u 2097152 -w 8 -T 0xC00FF022 \
  -P2 --start-graph --hold-ms 5000 -Q2 8 -f 1
```

`--hold-ms` is only useful in non-interactive owner mode. In interactive mode the
prompt keeps the process alive until `exit`.

### Cleanup

On `exit` or process termination through the normal cleanup path:

```
owner graphs opened by this app:
  pcm_stop, if started
  disconnect stream from audio interface
  pcm_close

shared memory:
  munmap app virtual address
  ShmemFree using spf_mem_handle
  close ion_fd

mixer:
  mixer_close
```

External graphs are not stopped or closed by `agm_shared_memory_test` because
they are owned by the external app that opened them.
